# promise: #609
# A space's ⌘T suggests archived tabs and visited pages from its own profile only (#609): Home is on
# Default and Work on another profile, each with an archived tab and a visited page. Before, Home's bar
# offered Work's too, so one profile's browsing was searchable from the other. A page in history from
# before Cra kept profiles (old-visit) is still suggested on both. The archive's Library page keeps
# every space's, as Arc's does (CommandBarProfileScope).
budget rss=600 stalls50=10
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
profile ${FIXTURES}/TwoProfiles
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=home
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1
wait 1
cra://commandbar?query=sieve
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=home
expect-log Cra command bar rows home: .*home-closed\.example\.com
expect-log Cra command bar rows home: .*home-visit\.example\.com
expect-log Cra command bar rows home: .*old-visit\.example\.com
reject-log Cra command bar rows home:.*work-
cra://dismiss
wait 1
cra://commandbar
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=home-empty
reject-log Cra command bar rows home-empty:.*work-closed
cra://dismiss
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=work&space=A0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
wait 2
cra://commandbar?query=sieve
wait 1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=work
expect-log Cra command bar rows work: .*work-closed\.example\.com
expect-log Cra command bar rows work: .*work-visit\.example\.com
expect-log Cra command bar rows work: .*old-visit\.example\.com
reject-log Cra command bar rows work:.*home-
cra://dismiss
